    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d347-a1">

                <pb facs="0473" n="389" xml:id="pg389"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister of Foreign Affairs to Mr.
                    Swenson.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Copenhagen</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1903-11-19"><hi rendition="#italic">November 19,
                        1903</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Mr. Minister</hi>: The King, my august soverign,
                    deeply sensible of the honor which the President of the United States of America
                    has shown him by expressing, through you, his hearty felicitations and best
                    wishes on the occasion of the fortieth anniversary of His Majesty’s reign, has
                    charged me to ask you to convey to Mr. Roosevelt His Majesty’s most sincere
                    thanks.</p>
                <p>Be pleased, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Deuntzer.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
